A||N||3||Patrick86GT||Rack bushing||||1||
Z||000000||Patrick86GT||07-03-2001||04:40 PM||||Has anybody replaced pass. side bushing on 88 GT rack and pinion?  Does the rack remain on the car? Any clues, pitfalls, hints?||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||07-03-2001||05:01 PM||||Mine was already off when I did it, but you can do it on the car. The first time I got another plastic one from Pontiac. It still wasn't real tight but did get rid of the bumping noise. Recently I got the aluminum one from Rodney Dickman. It has a lot less play than even the new plastic one. It comes with instructions and small rivets to hold it in. <P>I drilled and tapped the housing and used set screws instead of the rivets. I also drilled a hole and added a grease fitting. I don't think my extra stuff was really neccessary, just seemed like extra insurance.<P>Oh, on the car or off... take the spare tire tub out before working on it. The extra space is WELL worth the few minutes it takes to remove it!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Patrick86GT||07-03-2001||05:40 PM||||DRH, thanks for the tips. Embarassed to say that I did not open my Rodney Dickman bushing box yet...would have seen the instructions!  The spare tire tub is something I would not have thought of. Sounds like a good attack.<P>Any idea of time required if left on the car?||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||07-03-2001||06:01 PM||||Hard to say. Seems like I spend half my time looking for a tool I just had and the other half fixing something else I noticed while doing the original job.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  2 or 3 hours would be my guess if everything goes reasonably well.<P>Oh, just thought of another tip. I reused the bellows clip (twice now). I used a screwdriver to open the crimped part up. I used some (sideways for lack of a better term) wire cutters to carefully re-crimp without cutting.<P>The inner tie rod can be a real bear to break loose. I used a crescent wrench, a pipe wrench and a pipe for leverage. Be sure to re-lock the inner tie rod back in place when you put it back together (You'll see what I mean if you don't already know).<P>||||reg||1
